Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix: delete the Counter Claim stub, the actual collision
 was worse than a name clash
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Went looking for "just delete the stub route" and found the collision
was already live: PackageTeaserCard (src/components/library/) had its
own H2 saying "Reputation Manager" — but its href, alt text, and body
copy all still said "counter-claim", describing RM's real feature set
(46-prompt AI engine, Schema.org/Wikidata, crisis triggers) under the
wrong internal name and pointing at the wrong route. It had zero
importers anywhere in the app — a previous rename attempt that got
abandoned mid-way and left as dead, self-contradictory code.

Removed every trace of the Counter Claim placeholder (a different,
unbuilt chargeback/dispute product, not Reputation Manager):
- Deleted /dashboard/library/counter-claim/page.tsx and the unused
  PackageTeaserCard component.
- Removed its entry from copy.ts's WORKSPACE_PRODUCTS (the home page's
  product picker) — the array now lists Showtime and Reputation Manager,
  the only two real products.
- Removed the now-dead "counter-claim" filter in the workspace-creation
  page and the now-dead counter-claim branch in the home page's
  PackageBadge (both handled an id nothing installs anymore).
- Updated home-page.test.tsx's coming-soon test into real coverage for
  Reputation Manager's own card instead of asserting behavior for a
  product no longer in the list.
- Genericized two comments (schema.ts, workspace.ts) that used
  "counter-claim" as their example id.

Left alone: landing-wrapper.tsx's public marketing nav still has a
"Counter Claim" hover-menu item. It's decorative only (no link, no real
content — the dropdown lists generic sales-automation copy unrelated to
either product) on the pre-login marketing page, not a functional
collision — renaming or removing that copy is a marketing-content call,
not a code cleanup one, so flagging it rather than changing it myself.

